# One hailstone step in dc, the reverse-Polish desk calculator from 1971,
# older than C itself. Registers e and o hold the two branches as macros.
[2/]se
[3*1+]so
# Read n, and remember its parity in register p.
?d2%sp
# dc's only control flow: run a register's macro if two numbers are equal.
lp0=e
lp1=o
p
